        <div class="lvn-card__body">
          <p>Created using advanced technology that recreates the natural conditions under which diamonds form.</p>
          <p>Two methods are used: <strong>CVD (Chemical Vapour Deposition)</strong> and <strong>HPHT (High Pressure High Temperature)</strong>. Both start with pure carbon and apply intense heat and pressure to develop the same crystalline structure found in natural diamonds.</p>
          <p>The result is a diamond that is chemically, physically, and visually identical to a mined diamond. It has the same hardness, brilliance, and durability — and is graded using the same international standards.</p>
          <p>In simple terms, the difference is not what the diamond is, but where it comes from.</p>
        </div>
